<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  THE PAGE BEING COVERED, on a push. The fourth of four legs, and the one the app
  went without for so long that its absence became a reported defect.

  A STACK SLIDES AS ONE SHEET. Pushing, the arriving page comes from +16 and the page
  it covers goes to −16: both travel LEFT, together, and the eye reads one movement.
  Popping, both travel RIGHT (subpage_pop_enter.xml + subpage_exit.xml).

  What the app did instead was reuse ONE pair in both directions — subpage_enter for
  whichever activity was arriving and subpage_exit for whichever was leaving, on the
  reasoning that "the arriving screen always enters and the leaving screen always
  exits". That is true of the alpha and false of the translation. It made the covered
  page travel to +16, i.e. RIGHT, while the page arriving on top of it travelled LEFT:
  two 16dp movements crossing each other inside 260ms. On the way back it was the same
  crossing mirrored, and that one is not hidden behind an opaque incoming window, so
  that is the one the owner saw:

      «когда заходишь во вкладку какую-то и выходишь назад, то анимация выхода она типа
       дерганная как будто резко влево вправо делает и выход, хотя должно сбоку
       закрываться как-то»

  He is describing two things moving opposite ways and reading it, correctly, as one
  thing stuttering.

  Timing is subpage_exit.xml's, unchanged: @integer/motion_subpage_exit 195 = 75% of
  enter (00-rules.md 3.7, 8.5) on @interpolator/ease_standard, because leaving is a
  two-way state change the eye is not following. Only the DIRECTION differs, and that is
  the whole point of the file.

  API floor: fromXDelta/toXDelta only resolve a TYPE_DIMENSION from API 29
  (Animation.Description.parseValue). minSdk is 24, so on 24-28 the delta reads 0 and
  this degrades to the 195ms fade — correct tempo, correct curve, one channel short. It
  degrades, it never breaks, and it degrades identically in all four legs, so the pair
  can never half-apply.

  Reduced motion: apply through ui/component/SubPage.kt, never by hand (00-rules.md 8.8).
-->
<set xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:duration="@integer/motion_subpage_exit"
    android:fillAfter="false"
    android:interpolator="@interpolator/ease_standard"
    android:shareInterpolator="true">

    <translate
        android:fromXDelta="0"
        android:toXDelta="@dimen/space_16_reverse" />


</set>
